Unfortunately, you would have to do a bit of programming for this I think: writing a loop etc.  Once you create this variable, however, the analysis can be done simply by running the weighted fixed effects regression.  Doing the difference-in-means within each strata and then aggregating is the same as running the weighted fixed effects regression with certain regression weights: see this paper http://imai.princeton.edu/research/FEmatch.html (section 2.2).  The weighted fixed effects can then be run with the software "wfe", which we developed. 

